# .reachability-allowlist — modules intentionally excluded from the dead-code gate
#
# Read by scripts/check_reachability.py --allowlist. An entry covers the named
# module AND everything beneath it.
#
# Two kinds of entry, and the difference matters:
#
#   EXEMPT  Correctly never reachable from `berb run`. Not debt, no clock.
#   PARK    Acknowledged debt on a 90-day clock. Every PARK entry carries a
#           revisit date and names what would un-park it. A module still
#           without a consumer at its SECOND review is deleted then, not
#           parked again — that is the two-strikes rule.
#
# Never add an entry to make CI pass. The gate exists to stop the surface
# growing silently; parking is how you account for something, not how you hide
# it. Full method and verdicts: tasks/dead_code_wiring_plan.md and the
# per-wave triage docs beside it.
#
# Groups are numbered D-NN. Closed groups are kept as a record.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
